02:12:51.630 --> 02:12:56.510
It's about open source, start-ups.

02:12:56.510 --> 02:13:01.050
And Sam Ramji will lead that up.

02:13:01.050 --> 02:13:06.639
Before I wrap, I want to really thank our
partners, our precious partners, all 150 of

02:13:06.639 --> 02:13:08.500
them on the floor.

02:13:08.500 --> 02:13:13.630
I really look forward to working -- running
into you on the showcase floor.

02:13:13.630 --> 02:13:20.920
And, personally, I also want to express my
deep appreciation to all the thousands of

02:13:20.920 --> 02:13:22.400
people in Google Cloud.

02:13:22.400 --> 02:13:23.849
I mean, you're amazing people.

02:13:23.849 --> 02:13:25.449
It's why I'm at Google.

02:13:25.449 --> 02:13:32.330
And the hard work you've done over the last
year, you know, and how smart and excellent

02:13:32.330 --> 02:13:37.870
your work is, much appreciation.

02:13:37.870 --> 02:13:40.409
I want to remind you we're going to take a
break.

02:13:40.409 --> 02:13:43.809
But at 12:30, we're going to have two real
Internet giants.

02:13:43.809 --> 02:13:51.280
I was a judge in the first Queen Elizabeth
prize for engineering.

02:13:51.280 --> 02:13:54.650
I think it's now in its third year.

02:13:54.650 --> 02:14:00.420
And Vint Cerf and Marc Andreessen were two
of the winners for inventing the Internet.

02:14:00.420 --> 02:14:02.300
Those two haven't skipped a beat.

02:14:02.300 --> 02:14:09.070
They're actively leading and defining our
world in technology and as an ongoing basis.

02:14:09.070 --> 02:14:15.590
They'll be here for a discussion with Quentin
Hardy.

02:14:15.590 --> 02:14:19.170
So with that, I'm really wrapping it up.

02:14:19.170 --> 02:14:20.540
It's been a long keynote.

02:14:20.540 --> 02:14:21.630
Thank you for staying.

02:14:21.630 --> 02:14:23.219
We really appreciate it.

02:14:23.219 --> 02:14:25.770
And, hey, everybody, enjoy the show.

02:14:25.770 --> 02:14:26.770
Thank you very much.

02:14:26.770 --> 02:14:26.771
